WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.240
How do
we see things around us?

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.270
You will probably say it is EYES that help
us to see the

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.920
objects around us.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.520
But will your eyes be able to see these objects
in dark?

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.700
No, we need LIGHT to see things!

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.829
Without light, we cannot see the objects!

00:00:21.829 --> 00:00:24.580
But
where is this light coming from?

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.680
This light is coming from this source which
is a

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.700
fluorescent bulb!

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.140
You see that this bulb is emitting its own
light.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.540
The objects
which emit their own light are called LUMINOUS

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:36.540
OBJECTS.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.170
Can you give me any
other examples?

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:45.770
Incandescent light bulb, the sun, the stars
are also luminous objects!

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:48.910
What about objects such as this table and
chair?

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.680
Do they emit their own light?

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.890
No, these objects do not emit their own light!

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.920
Such objects are called NON-
LUMINOUS.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.780
Almost everything around us is non-luminous.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:07.090
Objects made up of
wood, plastic, cotton, metal are all non-luminous!

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.479
What about the moon and the planets?

00:01:09.479 --> 00:01:11.590
They are also non-luminous!

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:14.380
But if the
moon is non-luminous, then how come we are

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.170
able to see it at night?

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:19.550
The answer to this is REFLECTION OF LIGHT.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:24.520
The reason we are able to see any
nonluminous objects around us is because of

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.520
reflection of light!

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.250
Reflection of
light can simply be referred to as CHANGE

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:33.300
IN DIRECTION OF LIGHT or bouncing
of light from some surface.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:38.680
Just like the ball bounces back from the ground,
light reflects off from a smooth surface.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.910
Let me try to explain this in a simple
way.

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:48.640
The light from the source strikes the object
and bounces off from its surface!

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:51.960
And when this light reaches our eyes, we see
that object!

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.310
And this is how we
see NONLUMINOUS OBJECTS!

00:01:56.310 --> 00:02:01.320
When the object is kept in front of the mirror,
its image is formed in it.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.500
But will
we be able to see the image in the dark?

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.950
No we won’t.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:10.659
So the formation of the IMAGE is also due
to reflection of light.

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:15.579
Let this object be our human body, so at the
same time we are looking at the

00:02:15.579 --> 00:02:16.769
image!

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:20.720
First tell me, is our body a luminous or a
nonluminous object?

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.599
Well it is
nonluminous!

00:02:23.599 --> 00:02:26.779
Human body cannot emit its own light!

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:31.390
So the light from the source is first incident
on the human body.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.419
It gets
reflected from it and this reflected light

00:02:34.419 --> 00:02:36.620
strikes the mirror.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.670
This light is further
reflected from the surface of the mirror and

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.749
reaches our eyes!

00:02:41.749 --> 00:02:44.819
This is how we
are able to see our image!

00:02:44.819 --> 00:02:47.840
Now obviously this is not exact picture of
the

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.090
happenings.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:53.260
I just wanted to give you the intuitive feeling
into how this

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.260
happens.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:57.359
There are lot of subtleties involved which
we will learn in our higher

00:02:57.359 --> 00:02:57.829
grades!

